------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing / #5 No-parity-shortcuts)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <BottomTabBar> is a PURE presentational PRIMITIVE. It renders a fixed `<nav aria-label=
t('nav.quickNav')>` of five `<PrefetchLink>` tabs (Dashboard / Drives / Charging / Battery / Map), tinting
the one whose route is active (theme-primary + icon drop-shadow + a bottom accent bar) and forwarding taps
through the router link. Its only inputs are `useLocation()` (the pathname) and `useTranslation()` (the
labels). There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO loading / error / stale /
offline branch (there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from; the routed pages own their data
states). Reproducing those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this
surface reproduces only the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition the accepted sibling
presentational primitives Accordion (0203), Label (0218), LinearSidebar (0174), ActiveFilterChips (0147),
and StaggerItem (0194) recorded. The REAL branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • active tab     : route matches a tab path (theme tint + glow + accent pill + .isSelected/aria-current).
  • inactive tab   : muted glyph + label (web text-[var(--text-muted)]).
  • no-active      : a route matching no tab (e.g. /settings) -> every tab inactive (the web's real case).
  • empty catalog  : the native never-a-blank-box leaf (the web TABS const is never empty -> defensive).
Active-path rule : the VERBATIM port of the web `tab.path === '/' ? pathname === '/' : pathname === to ||
                   pathname.startsWith(to + '/')` — covered by isActivePath tests incl. the sibling-prefix
                   guard (`/charging-history` must NOT activate `/charging`).
Data sources     : useLocation (web) -> the bound pathname (BottomTabBarInput, updated via .onChange — the
                   P1/S8 binding to the host router state); useTranslation -> the P1/S10 facade. No fetch.
Shared comps     : none (web imports only PrefetchLink + lucide icons + cn — chrome, not shared surfaces).
Charts/maps      : none (the web source uses neither) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
Nav target       : web `<PrefetchLink to={path}>` -> forwarded as `onNavigate(path)` (the web path strings
                   "/", "/drives", … verbatim; the host shell maps them to AppRoute, exactly as the accepted
                   LinearSidebar 0174 forwards `onNavigate(row.path)`).
Icons            : web lucide (Home/Car/BatteryCharging/HeartPulse/MapPin) -> nearest SF Symbols
                   (house.fill / car.fill / battery.100.bolt / heart.fill / mappin.and.ellipse).
i18n keys        : nav.quickNav, nav.dashboard, nav.drives, nav.charging, nav.battery, nav.liveMap — ALL six
                   web keys mirrored verbatim with their source fallbacks; + the native bottomTabBar.empty.
                   No English literals in Swift code (every string via the facade).
Telemetry        : view.opened emitted once with slug "BottomTabBar" (P1/S11).
a11y             : the nav is one container (children: .contain) labelled with the localized nav aria-label;
                   each tab is a button labelled with its title, carrying .isSelected when active (the spoken
                   peer of aria-current="page"); the glyph + accent pill are accessibilityHidden; Dynamic
                   Type via the design tokens; the active-tab transition honours Reduce Motion.

